            <ArticleTitle>Reproductive health and the environment: Counseling patients about risks.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>367-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3949/ccjm.83a.14070</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endocrine-disrupting chemicals (EDCs) are associated with reproductive complications such as infertility, pregnancy complications, poor birth outcomes, and child developmental abnormalities, although not all chemicals of concern are EDCs. Pregnant patients and women of childbearing age need reasonable advice about environmental contaminants and reproductive health.</AbstractText>
